    "title": "<p><strong>Table&nbsp;10.03</strong> Histological characteristics and molecular phenotype of breast cancer in <em>BRCA1</em> and <em>BRCA2</em> mutation carriers compared with those of sporadic breast cancer</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Imported from 5th edition<br><br>Source: Modified from 21336636, van der Groep P, van der Wall E, van Diest PJ: Pathology of hereditary breast cancer. Cellular oncology 2011, 34:71-88.",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 456.7pt; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"609\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Characteristic(s)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 348.5pt; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-right: none; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"465\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Typical findings in mutation carriers</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; border: none; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">BRCA1</span></em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">BRCA2</span></em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Clinical</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">More lung and brain metastases</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">More bone and soft tissue metastases</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Margin</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Well-demarcated, solid nests, no tubule formation</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">More often pushing borders</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Lymphocytic infiltrate</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Prominent lymphoplasmacytic infiltrate</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Less lymphoplasmacytic infiltrate than in <em>BRCA1</em> carriers, but more than in sporadic cancer</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 5; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Necrosis</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Often necrosis, fibrotic focus</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">May be present</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 6; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Lymphovascular invasion</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Often present</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Less common</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 7; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Grade</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">High histological grade</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Variable histological grade (mainly grade&nbsp;2 or&nbsp;3)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 8; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Histological types</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">IBC, IBC with medullary pattern, metaplastic</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">IBC-NST, tubular, cribriform, mucinous, classic/pleomorphic lobular</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 9; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">In&nbsp;situ cancer</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Little DCIS</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">More frequently present with DCIS alone</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 10; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Little LCIS</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">LCIS may be present</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 11; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Immunophenotype</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">ER&minus;, PR&minus;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">ER+, PR+</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 12; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">ERBB2 (HER2)&minus;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">ERBB2 (HER2)&minus;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 13; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Strong staining with MIB1</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Variable staining with MIB1</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 14; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Molecular type</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Triple-negative: ER&minus;, PR&minus;, ERBB2 (HER2)&minus;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span lang=\"PT\" style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext; mso-ansi-language: PT;\">Luminal&nbsp;A: ER+, PR+, ERBB2 (HER2)&minus;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 15; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Basal-like: CK5/6+, CK14+, or EGFR+</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">CK5/6&minus;, CK14&minus;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 16; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"7\" valign=\"top\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Gene expression</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Genes involved in proliferation, adhesion, angiogenesis, motility, transcription, DNA repair</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Genes involved in proliferation, adhesion, signal transduction, extracellular matrix production</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 17; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CK8/18&minus;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CK8/18+</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 18; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">EGFR+</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">EGFR+</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 19; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">p53+, very often <em>TP53</em> mutations</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">p53+/&minus;, ~50% <em>TP53</em> mutations</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 20; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Cyclin&nbsp;D1&minus;, cyclin&nbsp;A and cyclin&nbsp;E high</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Cyclin D1+, cyclin&nbsp;A and cyclin&nbsp;E variable</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 21; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">BCL2 low</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">BCL2 high</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 22; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"mso-ansi-language: FR;\">HIF1</span>&alpha;<span lang=\"FR\" style=\"mso-ansi-language: FR;\">+, p63+, P-cadherin+, caveolin-1+, vimentin+, laminin+</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">FGF1+, FGFR1+, FGFR2+</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">DCIS, ductal carcinoma in&nbsp;situ; IBC, invasive breast carcinoma; LCIS, lobular carcinoma in&nbsp;situ; NST, of no special type.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Based on data from <span class=\"Ref-ID\">{21336636}</span>.</p>",
